<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zuo Zongtang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1812">1812</a>–<a href="/years/1885">1885</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zuo Zongtang (1812–1885) was a Chinese statesman and general of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>. He helped suppress the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion</a>, founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fuzhou-navy-yard">Fuzhou Navy Yard</a> and crushed the Dungan revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaanxi">Shaanxi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gansu">Gansu</a>. From 1876 he led the Qing reconquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaqub-beg">Yaqub Beg</a>'s Yettishar, after which Xinjiang was made a province in 1884.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zuo-zongtang.jpg" alt="Zuo Zongtang" width="320" height="468" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boiarskii, Adolf-Nikolay Erazmovich · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zuo_Zongtang_1875.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
